{"assets":[],"contestId":"205","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/205/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"205A - Little Elephant and Rozdil"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem was the simplest in the problemset. All you need to do is just to sort all distances (keeping track on all indices). If the first two distances are equal, just output \"Still Rozdil\", otherwise output the index of the first element of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The complexity is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NlogN"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/205/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"205B - Little Elephant and Sorting"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you need to notice the fact (which can be proven, but it is almost obvious) that if you are doing some operation for interval from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (inclusive), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This is becuase when you add something to all right part the answer can't be worse. After that you need to go from left to right and greedly add appropriate number of turns."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The complexity is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N